  <div class="pd-content">
    <h2 class="pd-title">Cyber Liability Insurance</h2>
    <section class="pd-broker-note" aria-label="Insurance broker note">
      <div class="pd-broker-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</div>
      <div class="pd-broker-body">
        <span class="pd-broker-tag">From a licensed insurance broker</span>
        <p class="pd-broker-text">
          <strong>N2N Insurance Brokerage</strong> does not represent any single insurer — it <strong>independently represents the client</strong>
          as an FSS-registered broker (Reg. No. 2026-012201). We compare the wordings, rates and service of AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz
          to propose the <strong>cover and price best suited to your risk</strong>. Each insurer's full wording is provided at application and binding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="pd-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="pd-tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" role="tab">Overview</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" role="tab">Cover</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" role="tab">How to apply</button>
    </div>

    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>Cyber insurance covers the insured’s legal liability to customers and third parties for a <strong>data breach or privacy violation</strong>, and also indemnifies the company’s own <strong>incident-response costs and business-interruption loss</strong> following a cyber event.</p>
        <p>Typical triggers include hacking, ransomware, DDoS, phishing, system intrusion and insider leakage of personal or confidential data.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Third-party + first-party combined</strong>
            <p>One policy answers both customer/third-party damages and the company’s own response and outage losses.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Incident-response costs</strong>
            <p>Forensics, breach notification, call-centre, credit monitoring, legal and PR costs are covered from the early stage.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Business interruption</strong>
            <p>Loss of profit and extra expense during a network outage caused by a covered cyber event.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Ransomware / cyber-extortion</strong>
            <p>Cyber-extortion and ransom handling within sub-limits, subject to underwriting.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Online platforms</strong>
            <p>E-commerce and platforms processing payments and personal data at scale.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Manufacturers with OT/ICS</strong>
            <p>Factories and distributors whose OT/ICS systems are linked to production lines.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Sensitive-data handlers</strong>
            <p>Finance, healthcare and public bodies processing large volumes of sensitive data.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Any exposed company</strong>
            <p>Any business exposed to ransomware, phishing and external attacks.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered — Third-party</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Damages and defense costs for a privacy breach or loss of customer data</li>
          <li>Regulatory investigation defense and fines/penalties where legally insurable</li>
          <li>Media / network security liability to third parties</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>First-party losses</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Incident response: forensics, breach notification, call-centre, credit monitoring, legal and PR</li>
          <li>Business interruption and extra expense during a covered outage</li>
          <li>Cyber-extortion / ransom handling (sub-limited)</li>
          <li>Data and system restoration costs</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main endorsements</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>PCI fines & assessments</strong>
            <p>Payment-card brand penalties and assessments after a card-data breach.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Social engineering / funds transfer</strong>
            <p>Fraudulent payment instruction and funds-transfer fraud cover.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Contingent business interruption</strong>
            <p>Outage of an outsourced IT or cloud provider that interrupts the insured.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Prior known incidents or circumstances notified before inception</li>
          <li>Bodily injury / property damage (covered under CGL/PL)</li>
          <li>War, and failure of public infrastructure or utilities</li>
          <li>Loss aggravated by unencrypted devices or unpatched systems, subject to wording</li>
          <li>Betterment / upgrade of systems beyond pre-loss condition</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Written on a <strong>Claims-Made</strong> basis; a retroactive date applies</li>
          <li>Security questionnaire underwriting (MFA, backups, EDR, patching)</li>
          <li>Sub-limits typically apply to ransomware, BI and extortion</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Business profile</strong>
            <p>Industry, annual revenue and the volume of personal-data records held.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Security controls</strong>
            <p>MFA, backup regime, EDR/anti-virus, patch management, access control.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Claims history</strong>
            <p>Any past cyber incidents or circumstances that could give rise to a claim.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Cover required</strong>
            <p>Desired aggregate limit, sub-limits and IT / cloud outsourcing arrangements.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Limits apply on an aggregate basis and sub-limits cap specific covers</li>
          <li>Final terms, sub-limits and premium are confirmed after insurer underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>

